      "An image service keeps resized thumbnails in memory and, when full, throws out the one that has been used the fewest times. Implement `lfu_shelf(capacity, ops)` and return one result per operation.\n\nOperations, processed in order:\n- `[\"get\", key]`: if the key is on the shelf, the result is its value and the key's use count goes up by 1. Otherwise the result is `None`.\n- `[\"put\", key, value]`:\n  - If the key is already on the shelf, its value is replaced and its use count goes up by 1. The result is `None`.\n  - Otherwise, if the shelf already holds `capacity` keys, one key is evicted first: the one with the **lowest use count**, and among those with the same count, the one whose most recent use (a successful `get` or any `put` of that key) is **oldest**. Then the new key is stored with a use count of 1. The result is the evicted key, or `None` when nothing was evicted.\n  - With a `capacity` of `0`, nothing is ever stored and the result is `None`.\n\nA key that was evicted and is put again starts over with a count of 1. Stored values are integers.",
